{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfZnQ9AmM9p6gZ3Z8W38i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I rewrote the repair candidate with a different mechanism, and the self-check prints `OK`. It hasn't been through the novelty gate or the full convergence fit yet; those run at admission.\n\n**Why the first attempt failed:** it made the H/T balance penalty individual per person. That is the same idea as the existing model `individual_balance_ideal_alternation`, so it made identical predictions and was rejected as a duplicate.\n\n**The new model:** `length_scaled_ideal_alternation`, a refinement of the incumbent `ideal_alternation_with_balance`.\n- **What stays the same:** each person still judges a sequence against their own ideal switching rate, and a shared penalty still makes lopsided H/T counts look less random.\n- **The one change:** being off the ideal switching rate counts for more in longer sequences, as if it were evidence that builds up over more flips. Sensitivity to alternation is multiplied by ((length − 1)/7)^κ, where κ is fitted with a prior of Normal(1, 0.5). When κ = 0 the model is exactly the incumbent.\n- **Why this change:** the second critique finding, `short_seq_alt_agreement`, says people judge short sequences by alternation less than the incumbent predicts, compared with length-8 sequences. This change is aimed at that gap. It didn't pass the multiple-comparison correction (q = 0.136), so it's weaker evidence than the balance finding. I skipped the balance finding because that route already belongs to `individual_balance_ideal_alternation`.\n\n**Self-check result:** the model loads, has a finite log-probability, meets the data contract and finished the short smoke fit. Its ELPD-LOO on that fit was −1007.3, against −1008.5 for the incumbent on the current data. That smoke fit ran one chain of 100 draws, so it doesn't show a real improvement. The check also warned that the ELPD-LOO estimate is unreliable, with 5.3% of trials having a high Pareto k against a 1% tolerance. That may be the short fit, but it could also stop this model from being chosen as the winner even if it is admitted.\n\n**Remaining risk:** if the full fit puts κ very close to 0, the model would predict almost exactly like the incumbent and be rejected as a duplicate again. This is the slot's final attempt.\n\nAll three files are in `iter_2/candidate_4_repair_1/`:\n- `hypothesis.md`\n- `model_name.txt`\n- `candidate.py`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3013,"cache_read_input_tokens":59538,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3013,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b869d83-ec12-4545-86ae-64ba0c12a051","uuid":"86a0d9fd-9666-406b-ba7a-7dcabcaa5f18","timestamp":"2026-09-30T14:30:01.522Z","request_id":"req_011CfZnQ8Q7zxfPbAP5KhBQd"}
